  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Medicines for Malaria Venture</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Increase investment in chemoprevention; 2) Develop new fast acting molecules to support treatment of uncomplicated and potentially severe malaria; 3) Develop compounds active against laboratory generated resistant strains and field isolates.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UK Department of Health and Social Care (DHSC) funds outstanding global health research through the National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR). The NIHR provided support to the Medicines for Malaria Venture (MMV) to carry out activities relating to the development of new drugs to treat malaria.</narrative>
  </description>
